// THE FLOOR OF A ROOFTOP COURSE.
//
// Old School paints a course deck with a plain grey and no texture, and that is how it looks there:
// a flat slab. Dropped into 2006 Draynor it reads as a missing texture, because every roof around it
// is slate - which is the shingle texture roof2, the same one oldroof_greyslate retextures onto its
// own model. So the deck gets the slate rather than a colour, and a roof looks like the roof it is
// part of from the street as well as from on top of it.

[roofdeck_greyslate]
overlay=yes
texture=roof2


// AND THE FLOOR OF AL KHARID'S, which is a desert roof and not a slate one.
//
// Old School paints Al Kharid's walkable deck #505050 - a plain mid grey, distinct from the roof it
// sits on. Ours had it on `desertroof`, #fffff5, the same near-white 377 paints the roofs themselves
// with: so the deck and the roof were one unbroken pale slab with no texture on it, which is the
// flat untextured look that was reported, and nothing on the roof showed you where the course went.
//
// The colour is Old School's own. The texture is this build's, for the reason written above: a flat
// grey with nothing on it reads as a missing texture here, and stone_tiles is what a flat stone roof
// over a sandstone building wears.
[roofdeck_desert]
overlay=yes
colour=0x505050
texture=stone_tiles
